WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.590
Once upon a time in Romania, there were a
thousand and one jump scares.

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:08.960
That's one way to describe The Nun, the fifth
entry in The Conjuring horror film series.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:13.929
Based on the case files of paranormal investigators
Ed and Lorraine Warren, The Nun is chronologically

00:00:13.929 --> 00:00:18.970
the first chapter of the Conjuring story,
taking audiences back to 1952 for a few nights

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:20.140
of religious horror.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.110
The Nun is about more than just a Marilyn
Manson lookalike terrorizing a creepy church.

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:28.950
In fact, the movie weaves a web of connections
to every Conjuring universe movie that came

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:29.950
before it.

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:33.500
If you were too spooked by the final showdown
to pay that much attention to the "what" and

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.970
the "why", then relax.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.640
We're ready to break down what it all meant.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:42.410
Pop on your habits and your purple stoles,
and let's dive into the ending to The Nun.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:43.850
The foreshadowing

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:48.030
Something is off about the abbey of St. Cartas
when the protagonists first arrive.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:52.579
Father Burke and the novice Sister Irene are
there investigating the death of a nun, suspected

00:00:52.579 --> 00:00:53.890
of taking her own life.

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:59.020
Their inquiry is aided by a French-Canadian
expat named Maurice aka "Frenchie".

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:02.820
As for the nuns of the abbey, they seem to
be of no help, if they're around at all.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:07.100
The visitors from the Vatican are greeted
by the Mother Superior, an inhospitable hooded

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.439
host who's basically a nunnified Darth Sidious.

00:01:10.439 --> 00:01:13.619
Other than her, the place at first seems suspiciously
empty.

00:01:13.619 --> 00:01:16.360
It turns out that there's a good reason for
that.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.120
The God squad

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:22.560
It becomes clear early on that evil has taken
root within the abbey an impression that's

00:01:22.579 --> 00:01:26.069
confirmed when Irene meets some of the abbey's
shellshocked nuns.

00:01:26.069 --> 00:01:30.659
It appears that the sisters of the abbey have
spent centuries in constant prayer to keep

00:01:30.659 --> 00:01:34.030
a demon from entering the world through a
portal in the abbey, but it's starting to

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:35.430
look like a losing fight.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:40.649
As The Nun's final act kicks in, Irene is
enlisted to help pray the devil away.

00:01:40.649 --> 00:01:45.459
She's joined by an entire squad of nuns who
mean business, all praying like their lives

00:01:45.459 --> 00:01:46.459
depend on it.

00:01:46.459 --> 00:01:50.960
It's an awesome moment... but also completely
fake, as it's shortly revealed that none of

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:53.760
those nuns actually exist.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:55.680
Stop believing

00:01:55.700 --> 00:02:00.929
When Burke and Frenchie reunite with Irene,
their presence snaps the sister back to reality.

00:02:00.929 --> 00:02:04.049
She's not fighting off the demon nun with
a group of other Catholics.

00:02:04.049 --> 00:02:08.629
Instead, she's having an incredibly complex
vision, seeing what appears to be the last

00:02:08.629 --> 00:02:11.439
stand of the abbey's now-dead residents.

00:02:11.439 --> 00:02:16.700
Irene and Burke realize they have been alone
inside the abbey the entire time, save for

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:19.240
the demon Valak and its minions.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:22.819
It's revealed to the audience that the two
nuns from the opening scene were actually

00:02:22.819 --> 00:02:27.409
the final two nuns in the abbey, trying to
keep Valak from possessing a human and entering

00:02:27.409 --> 00:02:29.129
the world beyond St. Carta.

00:02:29.129 --> 00:02:34.660
They realize that the nun they're investigating
didn't die in sin she died in an act of sacrifice.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:39.280
With this truth revealed, it's time for the
final showdown with the big bad nun.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:42.560
"S--- just got real."

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.200
Bloody Hell

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:49.319
After steeling themselves for the final battle,
our holy heroes descend into the catacombs.

00:02:49.319 --> 00:02:53.670
There, Irene realizes the meaning of a vision
she's been having since childhood.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:58.090
A message in those visions "Mary points the
way" turns out to be a set of instructions

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:03.700
that are literally true, as she follows a
pointing Virgin Mary statue to a conspicuous

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:04.700
fake wall.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:09.579
Using the key from the movie's opening, the
trio unlocks a hidden door to a secret passage,

00:03:09.579 --> 00:03:13.319
revealing an ancient glass relic containing
the blood of Jesus Christ.

00:03:13.319 --> 00:03:18.189
Armed with this powerful weapon, the three
go deeper into the catacombs to confront Valak,

00:03:18.189 --> 00:03:20.670
and hopefully close off the abbey's gate to
Hell.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:24.549
Things go south when Irene literally stumbles
onto a trap.

00:03:24.549 --> 00:03:29.719
She's briefly possessed by Valak, until Frenchie
breaks the relic and smears the blood of Christ

00:03:29.719 --> 00:03:30.940
onto her skin.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:34.069
The move drives the demon away, but not without
a fight.

00:03:34.069 --> 00:03:37.630
Irene and Valak tumble into the water of a
flooded room.

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:41.989
Valak holds Irene underwater until she goes
limp, seemingly drowning her and then Irene

00:03:41.989 --> 00:03:47.290
spits the entire container of Christ's blood
onto Valak's face, grossing the demon out

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:49.690
so much that it decides to go back to hell.

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:51.920
"Did I get any in my mouth?"

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:53.040
"Oh my God!"

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.000
Evil persists

00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:00.079
When Christ's blood spills into the water
of the flooded room, Valak is overwhelmed

00:04:00.079 --> 00:04:01.640
by its holy might.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:05.719
The demon dissolves, and the rift is sealed
up in the process as well.

00:04:05.719 --> 00:04:07.829
Just like that, the evil has been banished.

00:04:07.829 --> 00:04:10.819
The heroes have apparently won… or so it
seems.

00:04:10.819 --> 00:04:15.220
The next day, as Frenchie prepares to transport
Burke and Irene back to the village he rubs

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:21.690
a hand across his neck, revealing a conspicuous
new sign of the inverted cross on his skin,

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:25.230
apparently marking him as being possessed
by something evil.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:29.720
That's right it looks like our heroes' victory
isn't so certain after all.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:33.330
After all that, the demon accomplished its
goal.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.330
Full circle

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:39.820
The movie cuts to 20 years later, revisiting
a scene from the very first Conjuring movie.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:43.630
It's revealed that the lecture the Warrens
were seen giving in that movie about a possessed

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:49.230
man named Maurice was the same Maurice we
know better as Frenchie, possessed by Valak.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:50.720
"She saw something."

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:04.120
During the encounter, Valak touches Lorraine
and triggers within her the vision of Ed dying

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:06.750
that haunted her all throughout The Conjuring
2.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:11.000
Turns out, the visions the Warrens had of
the demon nun in that movie all came from

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:15.560
this encounter with Maurice, meaning their
climactic battle was set into motion before

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:18.450
the events of the first movie had even happened.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:22.840
Just like that, the movie ties the whole series
together, drawing a straight line from the

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:27.780
events at St. Carta to the Warrens' final
showdown with the demented demon, making The

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:32.710
Nun and the two Conjuring movies a complete
story about 30-year struggle between the forces

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:33.460
of good and evil.

